        "body": "Wednesday 2026-10-21 follow-through on dated real-world name-collision observations from Publication Discovery PR #3. This changes the **original Koios public renderer**, not a detached GEO score or keyword doorway page. The homepage's existing NewsMediaOrganization object now has a stable canonical `https://koios.news/#publisher` ID, paired with a WebSite `https://koios.news/#website` identity and explicit publisher reference. Actual NewsArticle `publisher` values refer to the same canonical publisher while retaining the already-shown name, URL, logo, and existing byline/source evidence. One native end-to-end build test checks the homepage and article output agree. No `sameAs` or corporate relationships are invented. No owner or legal identity is inferred from hosting. This is source-level semantic coherence, not evidence of changed Google ranking, public release, or an actual model citation. **Receive:** full original installed tests and site-build CI; then exact release and public readback by original Koios site release authority. Independent newsroom editorial gates, corrections, and article text are unchanged.",
